# Embedded C Patterns

## Volatile Usage
Use `volatile` for:
- Memory-mapped registers
- Variables shared with ISRs
- Variables modified by DMA

## ISR Rules
1. Keep ISRs SHORT
2. No printf/malloc/blocking calls
3. Clear interrupt flags appropriately
4. Use `volatile` for shared variables

## Defensive Programming
```c
if (ptr == NULL) return ERR_INVALID_PARAM;
if (index >= ARRAY_SIZE) return ERR_OUT_OF_RANGE;

uint32_t start = get_tick();
while (!(REG & FLAG)) {
    if (get_tick() - start > TIMEOUT_MS) return ERR_TIMEOUT;
}
```
